I was in one of the shops in the Gnomish mines. My cat wasn't cooperating by
stealing stuff, but it finally brought an item to the door. I threw it a tripe
ration when it was 2 squares into the shop. It didn't eat it. I step into the
shop to pick it up as well as a towel (both unpaid) and the shopkeeper didn't
move to block the door. I had been hasted quite a bit earlier but I thought
it would have worn off by now. I moved to the doorway and the shopkeeper asked
me to pay. Well I did, but it didn't take into account the gems I broke while
kicking a chest. I exited without knowing I owed, and got the usual Keystone
Kops. Only one of them attacked me and the others milled around. I didn't have
conflict, but they acked like it (I don't think they fought each other though).

I left the shops area so I couldn't be surrounded. I tried to pay before I left
but couldn't. I tried to pay a watchman, but he didn't want the money. I
accidentally hit one and had to fight him. I killed two of them and a Keystone
Cop before the shopkeeper axed before I could pay him.

1) Why didn't the cat eat the tripe?
2) Why did the shopkeeper not block the door?
3) Why didn't the Cops gang up on me?

It was really weird. I thought I was going to get away. I wasn't hasted when
I died. I had transgressed and was unlucky (I guess for killing the watchmen).

Oh, on a different note (and in a different game), I found both a sword named
Vorpal Blade and Sunsword in the same shop. I don't know if these were the
real things, but they were expensive 2000GP each. My cat stole Sunsword for me.
What does this do? It said I am charged (or something like that) with
Sunsword's power when I wielded it. It didn't seem to do much, but I never
tried #invoking it.

